rn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). Because of this, the check that `2.665` rounds to `2.66` in `tests/test_money.py` failed.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so I went by the test and the docstring. The PR hasn't been merged. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}